   {
    "id": "i8",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     91,
     102
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests {@link BinaryCodec#decode(Object)} across a range of ASCII binary strings. <p>Single-byte cases: bits are activated one at a time from LSB (bit 0) to MSB (bit 7), so each successive string has one more '1' on the right. <p>Two-byte cases: the low byte (index 0) always has all bits set; the high byte (index 1) gains bits incrementally from LSB to MSB, so the 16-character string gains a leading '1' each time. <p>Null case: a null input must yield an empty byte array."
   },
